    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d556">

                <pb facs="0603" n="589" xml:id="pg589"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/8–1944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 17461</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-19">August 19,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received August 24.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my despatch No. 16875 of
                    July 13<anchor n="6" xml:id="d556-f1"/> concerning the disposition of certain
                    construction equipment to the Brazilian Government, I have the honor to enclose
                    copy and translation of a communication from the Minister of Transportation and
                    Public Works, General Mendonça Lima,<anchor n="6a" xml:id="d556-f2"/> stating
                    that the new proposal, as Set out in my letter to him of July 13, a copy of
                    which was forwarded to the Department annexed to my despatch under reference,
                    has been entirely accepted by President Vargas and that funds will be made
                    available to take care of the expenses involved in accordance with the terms of
                    our proposal. I have informed General Wooten of this. It would be appreciated if
                    this information could be transmitted to the War Department.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jefferson Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
